    "category_specific_evidence": [
      "The NaN enters through the right operand: a Quantity holding nan with a time unit (np.nan * u.s or u.Quantity(np.nan, unit=u.s)) compared against TimeDelta(1, format='sec') or TimeDelta(5, format='sec').",
      "The fix renames TimeFormat._check_val_type to _check_finite_vals, with the comment that val1 cannot contain nan but val2 can, using np.isfinite checks on the inputs.",
      "A new class attribute _check_finite = True is added to TimeFormat, documented as checking that numeric inputs are finite (not nan or inf), and overridable in subclasses where nan and inf are valid inputs.",
      "The regression test test_time_delta_comp_nan_quantity expects dt1 < dt2, dt2 > dt1, dt1 <= dt2, dt2 >= dt1, dt1 > dt2, dt2 < dt1, dt1 >= dt2 and dt2 <= dt1 to all be False, and dt1 != dt2 to be True with dt1 == dt2 False, for dt2 = np.nan * u.s.",
      "The companion test test_time_delta_comp_num_quantity checks ordering and equality against 2 * u.s and expects ordinary boolean results.",
      "Issue #15230 reports the TypeError ('<' not supported between instances of 'TimeDelta' and 'Quantity') instead of the expected False, and the PR is #15830.",
      "The passages do not discuss +/-inf, signed zero or subnormal values; the special value involved is NaN only."
